rs/differential/14063607/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bb688b48a9bdf9433f9615488a54286d01373953bd06f951b1da89867ecf885"} {"question" "q-98231" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $f(x,y)$ varies with both $x$ and $y,$ which of the following **cannot** be the slope field for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bb688b48a9bdf9433f9615488a54286d01373953bd06f951b1da89867ecf885"} {"question" "q-98231" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is a function of $x$ and $y.$ This means that the slope field varies with both $x$ and $y.$\n\nOf the given slope fields, we note the following slope field does not vary with $x$ given a fixed value of $y.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/assets/43d4b05227a0667420e6978f01671931fb2392fe39692400407708edc8c24987.png)\n\n \n\nTo see this more clearly, notice that if we draw a horizontal line, the slopes do not vary.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/assets/718f65dc7f4ccab0931d04855c647bd39beffc014f1f389896edf83352fcc988.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bb688b48a9bdf9433f9615488a54286d01373953bd06f951b1da89867ecf885"} {"question" "q-98231" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1d9b76d77a148854d4f5c6b4fe5c9301aeea4cb46c3cd2008fcb17433597f34d"} {"question" "q-98231" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bb688b48a9bdf9433f9615488a54286d01373953bd06f951b1da89867ecf885"} {"question" "q-98231" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/assets/4191f22560c393dacad29a06e34b7c725800e27554e2c4ad7a9e40d9e56741e6.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/assets/43d4b05227a0667420e6978f01671931fb2392fe39692400407708edc8c24987.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/assets/58a69833c7b4f627c0cfd436f5ff624ea15dfc0f68d548e94b987794f06a58a0.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/assets/ab73df79e9518f68e27860a1655867d092255e604666c4153f3d950b30410fc5.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/assets/e45b8a64f56d831392ddc1eca4ddec922949d58e1c3f1f69c4db6238fe9a3200.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bb688b48a9bdf9433f9615488a54286d01373953bd06f951b1da89867ecf885"} {"question" "q-98231" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/assets/43d4b05227a0667420e6978f01671931fb2392fe39692400407708edc8c24987.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bb688b48a9bdf9433f9615488a54286d01373953bd06f951b1da89867ecf885"} {"question" "q-119774" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=8{x}^{2}{y}^{2}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bb688b48a9bdf9433f9615488a54286d01373953bd06f951b1da89867ecf885"} {"question" "q-119774" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we define $f(x,y)=8{x}^{2}{y}^{2}.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/assets/d1e4f48450a7f2032d755a5255d1a1e8a726dd16d273dae5dc1e587826d5ce58.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bb688b48a9bdf9433f9615488a54286d01373953bd06f951b1da89867ecf885"} {"question" "q-119774" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1d9b76d77a148854d4f5c6b4fe5c9301aeea4cb46c3cd2008fcb17433597f34d"} {"question" "q-119774" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bb688b48a9bdf9433f9615488a54286d01373953bd06f951b1da89867ecf885"} {"question" "q-119774" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None of those listed"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bb688b48a9bdf9433f9615488a54286d01373953bd06f951b1da89867ecf885"} {"question" "q-119774" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063607/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bb688b48a9bdf9433f9615488a54286d01373953bd06f951b1da89867ecf885"}] "usage" {"q-96767" []} "basis" 2056 "retractions" [[17592186172571 :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n2. At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n3. At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive"] [17592186172571 :question/worked-solution "The factor $2$ is positive, so the sign of $2xy$ is the sign of $xy$. It is positive in quadrants I and III and negative in II and IV. Thus I and III are true, while II is false. Select **I and III only**."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186171392 17592186171393 17592186171394 17592186171395 17592186171396] "immutable_fields" [[17592186171391 :answer-field/correct] [17592186171391 :answer-field/id] [17592186171391 :answer-field/key] [17592186171391 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
